  "description": "HarfBuzz text shaping for DocWright, for the complex scripts the built-in engine does not shape: Devanagari and the rest of Indic, Thai, Khmer and others, which are otherwise drawn one glyph per cluster and reported as DXP2002. Latin, Cyrillic, Greek, Arabic and Hebrew do not need it: DocWright shapes Arabic and Hebrew itself. The one DocWright package with a native dependency (HarfBuzzSharp; Linux hosts also need HarfBuzzSharp.NativeAssets.Linux), which is why it is opt-in.",
